{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-109552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The third-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,{y}^{″}-6t{y}^{′}-9y=t\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t)$ and ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-109552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},$ ${x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,{y}^{″}+6t{y}^{′}+9y+t.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,{x}_{3}+6t{x}_{2}+9{x}_{1}+t.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=9{x}_{1}+6t{x}_{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,{x}_{3}+t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nf(t)=9{x}_{1}+6t{x}_{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,{x}_{3}+t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-109552" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "07e711ffadb728da3c7806c7fe2064f4196fef19a7318b21b3404945dfe54a5d"} {"question" "q-109552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-109552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-9{x}_{1}-6t{x}_{2}-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,{x}_{3}-t"] ["math" "-\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-6t{x}_{2}-9{x}_{3}+t"] ["math" "9{x}_{1}+6t{x}_{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,{x}_{3}+t"] ["math" "9{x}_{1}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,{x}_{2}+6t{x}_{3}+t"] ["math" "\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}+6t{x}_{2}+9{x}_{3}-t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-109552" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "9{x}_{1}+6t{x}_{2}+\\operatorname{ln}⁡t\\,{x}_{3}+t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-107932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The third-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}-\\sqrt{t}\\,{y}^{″}-y={t}^{2}\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t)$ and ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-107932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},$ ${x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=\\sqrt{t}\\,{y}^{″}+y+{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}=\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3}+{x}_{1}+{t}^{2}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={x}_{1}+\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3}+{t}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nf(t)={x}_{1}+\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3}+{t}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-107932" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "07e711ffadb728da3c7806c7fe2064f4196fef19a7318b21b3404945dfe54a5d"} {"question" "q-107932" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-107932" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}+{t}^{2}"] ["math" "-{x}_{1}-\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3}-{t}^{2}"] ["math" "\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+{t}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}+\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3}+{t}^{2}"] ["math" "{x}_{1}-\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{2}+{t}^{2}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-107932" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{x}_{1}+\\sqrt{t}\\,{x}_{3}+{t}^{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/