s, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t)$ and ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-109534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{″}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}={t}^{2}{y}^{′}+t+1.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}={t}^{2}{x}_{2}+t+1.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={t}^{2}{x}_{2}+t+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nf(t)={t}^{2}{x}_{2}+t+1.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-109534" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "07e711ffadb728da3c7806c7fe2064f4196fef19a7318b21b3404945dfe54a5d"} {"question" "q-109534" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-109534" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-t{x}_{1}+{t}^{2}{x}_{2}+1"] ["math" "-{t}^{2}{x}_{2}-{x}_{2}+t"] ["math" "t{x}_{1}+{t}^{2}{x}_{2}+1"] ["math" "{t}^{2}{x}_{1}+t+1"] ["math" "{t}^{2}{x}_{2}+t+1"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-109534" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{t}^{2}{x}_{2}+t+1"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-109547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The third-order differential equation \n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}-{y}^{″}+3{y}^{′}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,y=2t\n$$\n\ncan be written as a system of first-order differential equations, as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=f(t)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere ${x}_{1}(t)=y(t),$ ${x}_{2}(t)={y}^{′}(t)$ and ${x}_{3}(t)={y}^{″}(t).$ Find the function $f(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-109547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we make the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}(t) & =y \\\\ {x}_{2}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{3}(t) & ={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{″} \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}(t) & ={y}^{‴}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as \n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}={y}^{‴}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAt this point, we're almost done. We just need to write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1},$ ${x}_{2},$ and ${x}_{3}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{‴}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}={y}^{″}-3{y}^{′}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,y+2t.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{‴}={x}_{3}-3{x}_{2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}+2t.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={x}_{3}, \\\\ {x}_{3}^{′}=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+2t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally,\n\n$$\nf(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+2t.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-109547" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "07e711ffadb728da3c7806c7fe2064f4196fef19a7318b21b3404945dfe54a5d"} {"question" "q-109547" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-109547" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}-{x}_{3}-2t"] ["math" "-{x}_{1}+3{x}_{2}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{3}-2t"] ["math" "3{x}_{1}-\\operatorname{cos}⁡t+{x}_{3}+2t"] ["math" "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+2t"] ["math" "{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{3}+2t"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-109547" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+{x}_{3}+2t"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-330754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The second-order differential equation ${y}^{″}-5{y}^{′}+{t}^{2}y=t{e}^{t}$ can be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ where\n\n| $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,A=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-1}} | {{field-2}} |  | $\\,,\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-3}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | {{field-4}} | {{field-5}} |  |  | {{field-6}} |  |  |  |\n\nand for $y=y(t),$ we have $y={x}_{1}(t)$ and ${y}^{′}={x}_{2}(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-330754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to express the given differential equation as a system of first-order differential equations. Then, we write the system as a matrix equation.\n\nWe start by making the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{″}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=5{y}^{′}-{t}^{2}y+t{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=5{x}_{2}-{t}^{2}{x}_{1}+t{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=-{t}^{2}{x}_{1}+5{x}_{2}+t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this system as the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -{t}^{2} & 5\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ t{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-330754" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "07e711ffadb728da3c7806c7fe2064f4196fef19a7318b21b3404945dfe54a5d"} {"question" "q-330754" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-330754" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-330754" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-330754" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-330754" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "c