son" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-330741" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The second-order differential equation ${y}^{″}-2{y}^{′}+3y={e}^{t}$ can be expressed as the matrix equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t),$ where\n\n| $x(t)=[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}],\\,A=\\,\\,$ |  | $0$ | {{field-1}} |  | $\\,,\\,f(t)=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  | $-3$ | {{field-3}} |  |  | {{field-4}} |  |  |  |\n\nand for $y=y(t),$ we have $y={x}_{1}(t)$ and ${y}^{′}={x}_{2}(t).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-330741" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "We first need to express the given differential equation as a system of first-order differential equations. Then, we write the system as a matrix equation.\n\nWe start by making the following change of variables:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & =y \\\\ {x}_{2} & ={y}^{′}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDifferentiating the above equations with respect to $t,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={y}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich we can rewrite as\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2}, \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}={y}^{″}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe must now write the right-hand side of the last equation in terms of ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}.$\n\nSolving our original differential equation for the highest-order derivative $({y}^{″}),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=2{y}^{′}-3y+{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nThen, we substitute our new variables into the right-hand side of the above equation. This gives\n\n$$\n{y}^{″}=2{x}_{2}-3{x}_{1}+{e}^{t}.\n$$\n\nNotice that we do not include any derivative terms on the right-hand side. \n\nTherefore, our complete system of equations is as follows:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′}={x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}=-3{x}_{1}+2{x}_{2}+{e}^{t}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can represent this system as the matrix differential equation ${x}^{′}(t)=Ax(t)+f(t)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}^{′} \\\\ {x}_{2}^{′}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ {e}^{t}\\end{aligned}]\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-330741" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "07e711ffadb728da3c7806c7fe2064f4196fef19a7318b21b3404945dfe54a5d"} {"question" "q-330741" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-330741" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "1"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c846dc39001740d02f2ca1adfcf827d162e95a14cf757d2349903133274cea7e"} {"question" "q-330741" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14070598/state.json" "file_sha256" "c8